This is the root file system of USR/UX 2.
When compiled, it will be turned into a img file containing the kernel binary (/boot/kernel.bin) (it will also be bootable).

Directories of the FS:
lost+found - Unused recovery directory where a program (fsck) may add recovered files to (made by ext2 itself).
root       - /home, but for the root user.
home       - Similar to C:\Users or /home in Linux. A directory containing the files for each user.
boot       - Directory containing GRUB and the kernel binary.
var        - Unused
run        - Has a file titled "runlevel". Shows current kernel runlevel.
bin        - User binaries (ls, cat)
sbin       - System binaries (init, telinit)
etc        - System-wide configuration files
dev        - Shows devices such as mouse, keyboard and framebuffer.
usr        - UNIX System Resources. Contains the folders bin (User-made binaries) and include (/lib/tcc/include is used however)
lib        - C library and kernel module loading place (for later stuff, such as networking drivers)
tmp        - Temporary
